**1. Introduction to the CUDA Programming Model and the Optimization Goal**

CUDA (Compute Unified Device Architecture) is a parallel computing platform and programming model developed by NVIDIA that leverages the massive parallelism of Graphics Processing Units (GPUs). The fundamental optimization goal on modern GPUs is not merely to make individual threads execute faster, but to maximize the overall throughput of the device. This is achieved by efficiently utilizing the available hardware resources—streaming multiprocessors (SMs), memory bandwidth, and the
